.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt STAT 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm stat
.Nd display native object identity and metadata
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
For each path print kind, byte size, object read-only flag, filesystem id,
non-reused object serial, link count, and modification time in UTC, or
.Ql unknown
when absent.
These are ABSD fields; there are no owners, groups or mode bits.
.Pp
With an active file-server channel also print the covering mount and this
session's read-write or read-only access.
An ancestor leading to session mounts may have no covering mount and is
reported read-only.
The object flag and mount access are distinct restrictions.
.Pp
Paths resolve through this process's view and no metadata is modified.
Errors go to standard error; later paths are attempted.
There is no option parsing: dash-leading operands are paths.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 for successful inspection; 1 for any metadata or timestamp error;
2 if no paths are supplied.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
stat /etc/network.conf /home/operator
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr df 1 ,
.Xr ls 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
